    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` on the owner response: `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`util/ContactPreferences.java`** (new) \u2014 derives the preference following the repo's existing util idiom (matching how `MembershipLevels` treats email presence: non-null and non-blank).\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. (Left it as a plain `type: string` rather than an inline `enum` \u2014 the `spring` generator would otherwise emit a nested enum type that the String-returning mapper expression couldn't populate.)\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression populating `contactPreference` from `ContactPreferences.preferenceFor(owner)`, alongside the other computed fields.\n\nThe value is computed in the mapper, so it flows through every endpoint that returns an `OwnerDto` (both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create/list responses).",
